  "question": {
    "text": "Let the normals at points&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math> meet at the point <math><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The equation of the normal from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;(other than <math><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>)&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
